The line above my snip indicates what to type in-game to get the 
entry. [/ to access the database, n for no to 'specify unknown 
object by cursor?', amulet of yendor for the 'word'.] Hence 
Boudewijn's rather brusque response.

The data lives in different files depending on the platform you're 
using (and maybe compile-time options on that platform) - e.g. 
'nhdat' on Windows, the NetHack binary itself on Mac OS 9, 'data' 
on unix systems. 

